<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolesław II of Masovia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1251–<a href="/years/1313">1313</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Boleslaw II of Masovia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolesław II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a> was a Piast duke who received Płock when the Duchy of Masovia was divided in 1275, and later reunited most of Masovia under his rule. He was briefly Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> in 1288 and was married to a Lithuanian princess, which tied Masovia to its pagan neighbour. On his death his lands were again divided among his sons.</p></div>
